    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d226">

                <pb facs="0317" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/1986a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-17T15:00:00-04:00">November 17,
                            1943—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1225. For your information, Helsinki reports that Finnish press “accurately
                    representing Finnish people” is united in denunciation of terms of unconditional
                    surrender for Finland and “resolve to fight on to the end”, rather than accept
                    such terms.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d226-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d226-f1" n="42" xml:id="d226-f1-content">
                <p>The BBC’s broadcast of November 15, 1943, had quoted the Soviet Red Army
                    newspaper, <hi rendition="#italic">Krasnaya Zvezda</hi>, to the effect that
                    Finland must surrender unconditionally.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
